  "Id": 2868,
  "Title": "Professor Stephane Pradines Talks about the \"Journal of Material Cultures in the Muslim World\"",
  "NewsSubTitle": "AKU-ISMC Publications",
  "NewsSummary": "Editor-in-chief Professor Stephane Pradines explains how the Journal  has become the go-to publication for many people and fields.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassCBFDC6427F80413F814CA0DEF7B9E82D\"><p><br>Editor-in-chief Professor Stephane Pradines explains how the <em><a href=\"/ismc/publications/Pages/mcmw.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Journal of Material Cultures in the Muslim World</a></em> has become the go-to publication for field archaeologists, art historians, anthropologists, curators, scholars and students of material culture in Muslim contexts.\u200b<br></p><p><a href=\"http&#58;//www.aku.edu/ismc/people/Pages/stephane-pradines.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Stephane Pradines</a> is an archaeologist and Professor of Islamic Art and Architecture at AKU-ISMC in London. Professor Pradines was the Director of the excavations of the Walls of Cairo (Egypt) and many other excavations in the Indian Ocean and East Africa. He is a specialist of Islamic archaeology in Sub-Saharan Africa, Indian Ocean medieval trade and Muslim material culture of&#160;\u200bwar.<br><br></p>\r\n<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https&#58;//www.youtube.com/embed/AWrsu-JGsg8\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe><br></div>",
